# CelebBoard — Marketing Site Design System
# Direction: Cinematic Split

> The complete visual and technical reference for building CelebBoard's marketing website.
> A brand-film aesthetic: full-bleed imagery, sharp edges, asymmetric grids, editorial storytelling.

---

## 1. Design Philosophy

### Core Principle: "The Big Screen Moment"

CelebBoard exists to put wins on a screen. The marketing site should feel like that moment — cinematic, full-bleed, dramatic. Not a software brochure. A story about what it feels like when the whole office looks up and cheers.

Three design pillars:

1. **Cinematic framing.** Every section is a "shot" in a visual story. Full-bleed backgrounds, split-screen layouts, asymmetric image-text pairings. The page flows like a brand film, not a feature list. Sections bleed into each other with purpose.

2. **Sharp confidence.** Zero border radius anywhere. Every element has crisp, editorial edges — buttons, cards, images, containers. This is a deliberate choice that says "we know exactly what we are." It creates visual tension that soft-cornered SaaS sites lack. The exception: team member photo circles and small badges.

3. **Imagery as architecture.** Photos, product screenshots, and ambient textures aren't decorative — they're structural. The hero IS a photo. Feature sections alternate between full-bleed visuals and tight text columns. The product dashboard is shown in context, not floating in space.

### Aesthetic Direction

**Cinematic editorial.** Think: a sports documentary meets a design agency portfolio. Dark, moody hero with warm amber light leaks. Asymmetric grids that break the 3-column monotony. Sora font brings geometric sharpness with just enough warmth. Cream-tinted light sections avoid the sterile white of typical SaaS. Sharp 0px radius everywhere creates a magazine-quality editorial feel.

### What Makes This Different

| Typical SaaS Site | CelebBoard Cinematic Split |
|---|---|
| Centered hero text with rounded screenshot below | Full-bleed photo hero, text overlaid left, TV mockup floating right |
| 3-column feature grid, all same size | Asymmetric 60/40 and 70/30 image-text splits |
| 12-16px border radius on everything | 0px radius everywhere — sharp, editorial, confident |
| White backgrounds with colored accents | Warm cream (#FAF9F7) and stone (#F5F5F4) light sections |
| Decorative illustrations | Real product screenshots in context, ambient photography textures |
| Uniform spacing between sections | Sections that bleed into each other, some with zero gap |

