### Color Usage Rules

1. **0px border radius on EVERYTHING.** Buttons, cards, inputs, images, containers. The only exceptions: team member photo circles (rounded-full), pill badges (rounded-full), and the favicon/logo mark.
2. **Never use pure white (#FFFFFF) as a section background.** Use --surface-light-warm (#FAF9F7) as the default light background. White is reserved for contrast elements inside warm sections (e.g., a card on a warm-100 bg).
3. **Dark sections use true black (#0A0A0A), not blue-tinted slate.** This creates maximum drama and makes amber accents sear.
4. **Amber is surgical.** Never use amber for large fills. Use it for: overline text, CTA buttons, accent borders, step numbers, decorative rules, and photo warm-glow overlays.
5. **Photo overlays always use `rgba(0,0,0,0.65)`.** This ensures text readability on any background image.

### Gradient Definitions

```css
/* Hero: dramatic dark falloff for text overlay on photos */
--gradient-photo-overlay: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(0,0,0,0.85), rgba(0,0,0,0.4));

/* Warm light leak effect behind product screenshots */
--gradient-warm-glow: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 50%, rgba(245,158,11,0.15), transparent 70%);

/* Section transition: dark to warm */
--gradient-dark-fade: linear-gradient(180deg, #0A0A0A, #161616);

/* CTA ambient: very subtle amber tint on dark */
--gradient-cta-ambient: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 30%, rgba(245,158,11,0.08), transparent 60%);
```

