```

### Type Scale

| Token | Size | Weight | Line Height | Letter Spacing | Usage |
|-------|------|--------|-------------|----------------|-------|
| `hero` | clamp(2.5rem, 5vw + 1rem, 4.5rem) | 700 | 1.02 | -0.04em | Homepage hero headline |
| `h1` | clamp(2rem, 3vw + 0.5rem, 3.5rem) | 700 | 1.05 | -0.03em | Page titles |
| `h2` | clamp(1.5rem, 2vw + 0.5rem, 2.5rem) | 700 | 1.1 | -0.025em | Section headings |
| `h3` | clamp(1.125rem, 1.5vw + 0.25rem, 1.5rem) | 600 | 1.2 | -0.02em | Card titles, sub-sections |
| `h4` | 1.125rem (18px) | 600 | 1.3 | -0.01em | Small headings |
| `body` | 1rem (16px) | 400 | 1.65 | 0 | Paragraphs, descriptions |
| `body-sm` | 0.875rem (14px) | 400 | 1.6 | 0 | Captions, secondary text |
| `body-xs` | 0.75rem (12px) | 400 | 1.5 | 0 | Labels, meta info |
| `overline` | 0.6875rem (11px) | 700 | 1 | 0.2em | Section labels, categories — UPPERCASE |
| `display-num` | clamp(2rem, 3vw, 3.5rem) | 800 | 1 | -0.03em | Metric values, prices |

### Typography Rules

1. **Headlines are tight.** Letter-spacing goes negative on anything h3 and above. Headings should feel compressed, punchy — not airy.
2. **Body text breathes.** Line-height 1.65 for body, max-width 600px. Comfortable reading.
3. **Overline precedes EVERY section heading.** Always amber (#F59E0B), 11px, weight 700, uppercase, tracking 0.2em. This is the #1 visual rhythm device.
4. **Max two lines for hero headlines.** If it needs three lines, the copy is too long.
5. **No italics on headings.** The Cinematic Split direction uses straight geometry, not editorial serif curves.

