### Contrast Ratios (WCAG AA)

| Text | Background | Ratio | Pass |
|------|-----------|-------|------|
| #FAFAFA on #0A0A0A | Dark hero | 19.4:1 | ✅ AAA |
| #888888 on #0A0A0A | Dark muted | 5.5:1 | ✅ AA |
| #F59E0B on #0A0A0A | Amber on dark | 8.2:1 | ✅ AAA |
| #111111 on #FAF9F7 | Light heading | 17.1:1 | ✅ AAA |
| #666666 on #FAF9F7 | Light muted | 5.9:1 | ✅ AA |
| #0F172A on #F59E0B | Button text | 8.5:1 | ✅ AAA |
| #FFFFFF on #F59E0B | Alt button text | 3.1:1 | ⚠️ AA-large only |

**Note:** CTA buttons use dark text (#0F172A) on amber — not white on amber (which fails AA for small text).

### Focus States

```css
*:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid #F59E0B;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

/* On dark backgrounds */
[data-surface="dark"] *:focus-visible {
  outline-color: #FBBF24;
}
```

### Semantic HTML

- Every section landmark uses `<section>` with `aria-labelledby`
- Heading hierarchy: one `<h1>` per page, sections use `<h2>`, sub-sections `<h3>`
- Navigation uses `<nav>` with `aria-label`
- Images use descriptive `alt` text; decorative textures use `aria-hidden="true"`
- Buttons have meaningful text (never "Click here")
- Color is never the only indicator of state

### Touch Targets

- Minimum 44×44px for all interactive elements
- Navbar links: 44px tall tap zone even if text is smaller
- Mobile menu items: full-width, 48px tall minimum

