## 12. Quick Reference — Design Decisions

| Decision | Choice | Why |
|----------|--------|-----|
| Border radius | 0px everywhere | Editorial confidence, visual tension, uniqueness |
| Dark base | True black (#0A0A0A) | Maximum drama, amber pops harder than on blue-gray |
| Light base | Warm stone (#FAF9F7) | Gallery warmth, not sterile SaaS white |
| Font | Sora | Geometric + warm, wider letterforms than Inter, distinctive |
| Layout | Asymmetric 60/40 splits | Cinematic, storytelling, breaks SaaS monotony |
| Feature layout | Edge-to-edge with dividers | Feels like a magazine, not a card grid |
| Hero | Full-bleed photo + text overlay | Dramatic, cinematic, memorable |
| CTA | Dark + amber ambient glow | Warm ending, callback to hero mood |
| Accent usage | Surgical — overlines, buttons, rules, step numbers | Amber means something every time it appears |
| Photos | Always in context (TV mockup, office scene) | Product sells when shown as it's used |
| Team photos | Only rounded elements on the page | Humanizes, creates visual contrast with sharp edges |
| Gradient use | Photo overlays + warm glows only | No decorative gradients — this is photography-driven |

